I replaced the generic `SetFieldUINT8Value` call with direct construction of a `Field` and a call to `SetField`, bypassing the subfield/profile lookup logic inside the generic setter. This saves a function call and the associated branching for the common main-field case.

```cpp
    void SetAwakeningsCount(FIT_UINT8 awakeningsCount)
    {
        Field field;
        field.SetNum(11);
        field.SetSize(1);
        field.SetType(FIT_BASE_TYPE_UINT8);
        field.SetValue(&awakeningsCount, 1);
        SetField(field);
    }
```